<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reccared I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 586–601</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Reccared I was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> from 586 to 601, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liuvigild">Liuvigild</a>. In 587 he converted from Arian to Catholic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>, and at the Third Council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a> in 589 the Visigothic nobility and Arian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> followed him, ending the religious division between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a> and Hispano-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>. The Councils of Toledo then became a central institution of the kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/reccared-i.jpg" alt="Reccared I" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Numismática Pliego · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Recaredo_Tremis_Ispali.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
